  "changed_since_previous": "Clarified doc/JSON-RPC-interface.md table entries to explain HTTP status expectations for invalid JSON bodies and valid notifications, and adjusted UniValue push operations in the implementation.",
  "card": "This PR fixes JSON-RPC 2.0 specification compliance and prevents debug assertion crashes when handling malformed JSON-RPC 2.0 requests. Previously, malformed 2.0 requests (such as missing method names or invalid parameter types) triggered an Assume() assertion crash on debug builds when authenticated, or returned an HTTP 400 error in release builds instead of the standard HTTP 200 with an error object. It also ensures invalid requests lacking an ID are not treated as silent notifications in batch requests. No dependencies.",
